.policy "ruff-n811-constant-imported-as-non-constant" revision 3
.description "Keep the alias of an imported constant in UPPER_CASE; a lowercase or CamelCase alias makes readers mistake the constant for a variable or class."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N811 (pep8-naming): an UPPER_CASE name imported under an alias that is not UPPER_CASE. A one-character
// name may take a CamelCase alias (`from django.db.models import Q as Query`). Names are read NFKC-normalised and
// cased by Unicode: `Ǆ` is "DŽ", two characters. Exempt when the name or the alias matches
// `pep8-naming.ignore-names`. Ruff reads `import a.CONST as c` by its last segment.
//   from mod import CONSTANT as constant     ← N811
//   from mod import Q as Query               not reported
//   from mod import Ⅱ as Two                 ← N811: `II` is two characters
#include "python/python-19.rerail"

.violation N811(at: node, x: symbol, a: symbol) code "N811"
    "Drop `as {a}` or use an UPPER_CASE alias for the constant `{x}`, and update its uses; keep the alias if `{x}` is really a class."
    suppress ruff "N811"
N811(i, x, a) :- alias_import(i, x0, a0), x = @nfkc(x0), a = @nfkc(a0), pep8_cased_upper(i, x), !pep8_cased_upper(i, a),
    (!match(".", x) ; !pep8_camel(i, a)), !pep8_ignored(i, x), !pep8_ignored(i, a).
